#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059663 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059494 :question/id #uuid "7341638b-3c0f-5c10-8b7d-a2c313607bed" :question/math-academy-id "e-3519" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)$ without using a calculator.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $$\n\\displaystyle \\dfrac{\\pi}{12} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3} - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}.\n$$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y) = \\sin x\\cos y - \\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $x = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$ and $y = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "213eda96-c41d-5361-9da9-8349617014f1" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049923 :topic/id #uuid "1ed8dd8d-e728-5e57-81fe-a7c1a6a08469" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124481} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124482} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124483}] :topic/math-academy-id 1927 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048132} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048187} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048702} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048868} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048952} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049029} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049067} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049878} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049999} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050341} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050496}] :topic/title "The Product Rule for Radicals"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050848 :topic/id #uuid "6b88d999-b59b-5a3